`filterVolumes` performs a case-insensitive substring search over volume titles. Trim the query before matching. An empty or whitespace-only query matches every volume. Preserve input order and duplicates. Return a new array containing newly allocated volume objects so neither the input array nor its elements are aliased or mutated. IDs must be positive safe integers and titles must be nonblank after trimming; encountering any malformed volume throws `RangeError` before a result is returned. Matching uses each trimmed title, and returned titles are trimmed.

Known-bad source:

```ts
export interface Volume {
  readonly id: number;
  readonly title: string;
}

export function filterVolumes(volumes: readonly Volume[], query: string): Volume[] {
  const needle = query.trim();
  const normalized = volumes.map((volume) => {
    if (!Number.isSafeInteger(volume.id) || volume.id <= 0) throw new RangeError("id must be positive");
    const title = volume.title.trim();
    if (title.length === 0) throw new RangeError("title must not be blank");
    return { id: volume.id, title };
  });
  return normalized.filter((volume) => volume.title.toLowerCase().includes(needle));
}
```

